  "source": "Vanilla ElytraModel, standing pose. left_wing addBox(-10,0,0,10,20,2) at PartPose.offsetAndRotation(5,0,0, 15deg,0,-15deg); right_wing addBox(0,0,0,10,20,2) at (-5,0,0, 15deg,0,15deg); CubeDeformation(1), texOffs(22,0), 64x32. ElytraLayer renders it at pose.translate(0,0,0.125), so the slabs sit 2 px behind the torso's back face (Bedrock z=2). Java y runs down from the neck, so Bedrock y = 24 - java y. CubeListBuilder.mirror() only reverses the winding and flips the normal in ModelPart$Polygon; it does not mirror the UVs, so both slabs sample the same rectangle. The right slab carries a 0.25 px z nudge that only breaks the coplanar depth tie between the two wings."
